From f6dfc513c0c6947b41973b543b0be5b2f2718c34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kshot3000 <kshot9000@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:38:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(apps): repair pearl-address-validation package
 (tests, base58, docs)

- Remove the base58 branch: Pearl is Taproot-only (bech32m, witness v1+,
  32-byte programs; see node/btcutil/address.go decodeSegWitAddress) and has
  never had base58 addresses. The branch used Bitcoin version bytes
  (0x00/0x6f/0x05/0xc4), so e.g. a Bitcoin P2PKH address validated as a
  'valid Pearl address'. base58-js and sha256-uint8array deps removed.
- Fix the test suite: it referenced dup/td/duprt/sd HRPs that the
  implementation rejects, so 9/17 tests failed as published. Tests now use
  real prl/tprl/rprl bech32m vectors (mainnet vector is a known-good Pearl
  address) plus regression cases for v0, v2, short programs, bad checksums,
  wrong HRPs, base58, and mixed case. 19/19 pass.
- Rewrite the README, which documented Bitcoin-style base58 examples and a
  signet network the code does not implement.
